/**

@brief Platform Level Data Model tests
@defgroup tests_pldm PLDM
@ingroup all_tests
@details
PLDM (Platform Level Data Model) is the DMTF management protocol the PMCI firmware uses
to expose platform descriptor records, sensor readings and vendor-specific commands.
The tests in this area cover the firmware's PLDM implementation, split by the part of
the protocol under test.
@{
@}

@defgroup tests_pldm_mctp_transport PLDM MCTP transport
@ingroup tests_pldm
@details
PLDM carried over MCTP to the DMC firmware, exercised end to end. This covers the base,
platform and OEM message types as they arrive over the wire, and the DMC's responses to
them.
@{
@}

@defgroup tests_pldm_pdr_builder PLDM PDR builder
@ingroup tests_pldm
@details
Construction of the platform descriptor record repository from devicetree, and access to
the records in it by index, by record handle and by sensor ID. Chunked retrieval of
records is part of this scope.
@{
@}

@defgroup tests_pldm_platform PLDM platform
@ingroup tests_pldm
@details
The platform command set: repository information, descriptor record retrieval, sensor
readings, and discovery of platform versions and supported commands.
@{
@}

@defgroup tests_pldm_oem PLDM OEM
@ingroup tests_pldm
@details
Tenstorrent's vendor-specific PLDM type (0x3F), which provides a remote shell over PLDM:
starting a command, collecting its output, and cancelling it.
@{
@}

@defgroup tests_pldm_base PLDM base
@ingroup tests_pldm
@details
The base command set that every PLDM responder implements: terminus ID, supported types,
supported commands and versions.
@{
@}

*/
